the static locals and their guard, the divergence docs/CONFORMANCE.md records under "A static local keeps its own name in the object file": cxx1 spells one `<function's mangled symbol>.name` - `?f@S@@QEAAHXZ.n`, `??1S@@QEAA@XZ.d`, `main.n`, `?g@S@@QEAAHXZ.l` with `.l$guard` - where cl writes `?n@?1??f@S@@QEAAHXZ@4HA`, `?d@?1???1S@@QEAA@XZ@4HA` and the `?$TSS0@` guard; `_Init_thread_abort`, which cl calls from the unwind path if the constructor throws while the guard is held and cxx1 does not emit yet (static-local-constructor.nocl says the same); and the closure, `$_0` against `<lambda_0>`, which lookup-order.nocl records. File-local symbols, nothing links against them; that every one is a distinct object is what the case's output checks.
